docs/implementation/fixtures/ADJUSTMENT-RASTER-ACCEPTANCE.md:3:These artifacts prepare real browser/Tauri export comparison. They do not themselves prove any browser export passed. No product code is changed by their generation.
docs/implementation/fixtures/ADJUSTMENT-RASTER-ACCEPTANCE.md:5:Open `adjustment-colorcard-64.draivio` in Draivio. Its only layer (`card`) is an embedded 64×64 PNG at 100% opacity, normal blending, no transform, zero adjustments, preview enabled. Background is transparent, selection hidden, with no groups, masks, text, shapes, or strokes. Project decoding and offline encode/decode roundtrip are checked by the artifact test. Source `adjustment-colorcard-64.png` and unpremultiplied bytes `adjustment-colorcard-64.rgba` are adjacent.
docs/implementation/fixtures/ADJUSTMENT-RASTER-ACCEPTANCE.md:9:For each case, start from neutral (all-reset), leave preview enabled, set only the specified control, then export **PNG at original 64×64**. Do not scale, flatten onto an opaque background, transform, or combine settings. Native UI export/download must be performed and observed separately. Values and filenames:
docs/implementation/fixtures/ADJUSTMENT-RASTER-ACCEPTANCE.md:25:`adjustment-expected/manifest.json` records all exact parameters. Each case has deterministic CPU reference `.rgba` and a convenience `.png`; these PNGs are CPU outputs, not browser downloads. Expected pixels import production `applyLayerAdjustments` so changing that algorithm requires regenerating artifacts. Browser/CPU matching is what the comparison is intended to independently measure.
docs/implementation/fixtures/ADJUSTMENT-RASTER-ACCEPTANCE.md:36:Compare an actually downloaded PNG (absolute download path can be anywhere):
docs/implementation/fixtures/ADJUSTMENT-RASTER-ACCEPTANCE.md:42:Output contains max/mean/count/nonzero absolute channel deltas for all RGBA, RGB where both pixels have positive alpha, RGB where both are opaque, and alpha independently. It checks 64×64 dimensions and PNG CRC. It does not apply an invented tolerance or mark acceptance. Save the emitted JSON as evidence alongside the actual downloaded PNG, case, browser engine/version, app revision, and export settings. No downloaded browser PNG has been compared in this worker.
docs/implementation/fixtures/ADJUSTMENT-RASTER-ACCEPTANCE.md:50:The decoder uses Python standard library only. It supports noninterlaced 8-bit RGBA, RGB, grayscale, grayscale+alpha, and indexed PNG, all five PNG row filters. It returns decoded unpremultiplied channel bytes without color-profile conversion. Interlaced or non-8-bit output is rejected explicitly. Two decoder self-tests verify all five row filters against known independent bytes and verify source/neutral identity. Artifact validation and decoder self-tests passed; native export pixels and native performance remain pending.
docs/implementation/fixtures/ADJUSTMENT-RASTER-ACCEPTANCE.md:54:The main reviewer performed production IAB PNG downloads. ExportDialog's default background was white, so those downloads must be compared with CPU pixels composited onto white rather than transparent CPU RGBA:
docs/implementation/fixtures/ADJUSTMENT-RASTER-ACCEPTANCE.md:60:Three standard-library decoder/compositing self-tests pass. White composition reduces the neutral reference to exact identity and explains prior alpha differences; it does not explain clarity failures. The reviewer-provided 11 actual downloads were decoded offline in this worker. Observed full RGB maxima were 0 neutral; 1–2 for scalar adjustments; 2 blur35; 3 blur100; **35 clarity35 and 57 clarity70**. Clarity remains failed, with no tolerance relaxation. Raw local comparison output was saved in `/tmp/draivio-native-adjustment-white-comparisons.json` for the main reviewer.
docs/implementation/fixtures/ADJUSTMENT-RASTER-ACCEPTANCE.md:64:`adjustment-convolution-diagnostic.html` displays four embedded 64px SVG images and explicit “导出诊断 NAME” buttons. Buttons locally rasterize their image to white-backed 64px PNG via canvas, then download. Cases compare identical source and coverage treatment with a 25×25 sigma6 convolution, mathematically equivalent separable 25×1 then 1×25 convolution, 13×13 sigma3 convolution, and identity. The page uses embedded assets without network calls. It is a diagnostic artifact, not production acceptance. The main reviewer must operate those buttons via CUA and supply actual downloaded PNG paths for analysis; this worker does not operate a browser.
